ches the paired-comparison goal. If k-fold CV were preferred, replace the fixed test with 5-fold repeated stratified CV and pool fold metrics; we keep the fixed holdout per approved default because it preserves clean learning curves. |\n| A8 | Repeats = 5 seeds for sizes \u2264512, 3 seeds for sizes \u22651024 (approved default) | If equal repeats everywhere, use 5 for all sizes (cost \u2248 +8 fits/architecture); if 3 everywhere, use 3 (slightly wider small-n CIs). |\n| A9 | Cd units are dimensionless, ~0.2\u20130.35, no transform needed | If Cd spans several orders of magnitude or is a scaled quantity, re-express RMSE in the dataset\u2019s reported units; the power-law exponent is scale-invariant under log-log fit so H1 is unaffected, but reported RMSE magnitudes must carry the units. |\n| A10 | CPU-only execution is sufficient (design-only here; would hold under the described environment) | If a GPU/materially different toolchain were required, only the MLP runtime estimate changes; the protocol is identical. |\nUncertainties carried forward: exact N (A2) and the precise 26-parameter schema (A3, A5) are the two items that most affect the executed run and must be checked against the DrivAerNet++ card before any future execution; everything else is fixed by the approved defaults above.\n\n## 12. Summary of controls (checklist)\n- Fixed 80/20 stratified test holdout, never used for tuning (A7).\n- Equal per-architecture tuning budget on the validation slice; configs frozen across sizes (A6).\n- Identical nested subsets and seeds across architectures \u2192 paired comparisons (A7, A8).\n- Z-score fit on training subset only; validation/test never feed scaler or early stopping (\u00a75).\n- Deterministic seeds recorded per (architecture, size, seed).\n- H1 via power-law \u03b1 \u00b1 CI over a defined window with documented fit rule; H2 via mixed-effects interaction test + paired per-size tests with Holm correction.", "evidence": "Workspace inspection: /workspace contains only task.json declaring a design-only task (\u201cDesign-only task; repositories and compute are not required\u201d); filesystem-wide searches found no DrivAerNet/DrivAerNet++ data, no track.md, no data files (.csv/.parquet/.npz/.h5/.pkl/.npy), and no preinstalled ML stack (system Python 3.14.4; no sklearn/torch/pandas); network disabled; CPU-only with 224 cores. This confirms the design-only nature and that all dataset-level specifics (total N, 26-parameter schema, scalar Cd presence, Cd units, style encoding) are unverifiable locally and are recorded as assumptions in \u00a711 rather than asserted facts. The design resolves the researcher-approved defaults: RMSE primary with MAE/R^2/Spearman secondary; repeats 5 (sizes \u2264512) and 3 (sizes \u22651024); body style as one-hot + stratified splits with per-style metrics secondary; nested cumulative subsets shared across architectures per seed; tune-once-on-full-pool-and-freeze with equal \u226440-eval budgets per architecture; fixed stratified 80/20 holdout; explicit leakage controls (per-split z-scoring, no test-set tuning); mixed-effects log(RMSE) ~ log(n) + architecture + architecture\u00d7log(n) interaction test across shared seeds; dual-window power-law fit with per-architecture \u03b1 \u00b1 CI; CPU-only feasibility with bounded runtime estimates; and a limitations section covering the frozen-hyperparameter small-n caveat, single-dataset scope, and shape-model exclusion. No experiment was run or claimed.", "assumptions": ["DrivAerNet++ provides a tabular 26-parameter design vector and a scalar per-design Cd (A4; if only per-mesh values, aggregate to design mean).", "Total dataset size \u2248 7,000-8,000 designs, giving a dev pool of \u22485,600-5,760 for the 7-point scaling curve (A2).", "The 26 parameters are numeric design channels; categorical channels (incl. body style) are one-hot encoded before standardization (A3, A5).", "Body style (fastback/notchback/estateback) is available as a stratifying label and included as one-hot features (A5).", "Cd is dimensionless in the ~0.2-0.35 range; RMSE is reported in native Cd units (A1, A9).", "Primary metric RMSE; MAE, R^2, Spearman secondary (A1).", "Repeats: 5 seeds for sizes <=512, 3 seeds for sizes >=1024 (A8).", "Nested cumulative training subsets with identical subset per (size, seed) shared across architectures; fixed 80/20 stratified holdout (A7).", "Hyperparameters tuned once on the validation slice (<=40 evals per architecture) then frozen across sizes (A6).", "CPU-only execution (224 cores) is sufficient; MLP is the only architecture with material runtime (A10)."], "uncertainties": ["Total N and exact 26-parameter schema are the two facts that most affect an executed run and must be checked against the DrivAerNet++ card before future execution (A2, A3).", "Whether Cd exists as a per-design scalar or must be aggregated from per-mesh values (A4).", "Whether body style is embedded in the 26 params or a separate metadata column (A5).", "Power-law exponents are window- and metric-dependent; mitigated by the defined dual-window fit and documented fit rule, but remain descriptive of this dataset.", "Frozen hyperparameters may compress small-n absolute differences; flagged in limitations.", "Kernel ridge / GP scaling assumptions on N_dev (memory) are unverified; mitigated by random-search length-scale bounds and documented fallback to a subset-of-N kernel variant if memory pressure appears."], "summary": "Delivered complete DrivAerNet++ Cd surrogate scaling/architecture experiment design"}", "origin": "completion"}, "llm_response_id": "chatcmpl-9cee6365812245ee9eb931dcf6d74dda", "security_risk": "UNKNOWN", "critic_result": null, "summary": "Delivered complete DrivAerNet++ Cd surrogate scaling/architecture experiment design", "kind": "ActionEvent"}
